# NELA risk model, in the browser

`risk-score-service/src/risk-calculator.R` is supplied to us and is not
edited. This package compiles it, unchanged, for the browser: R itself
compiled to WebAssembly (webR) runs it in a Web Worker, so an ASC Audit
page works the score out in the background with no request to the service.

## How it is built

`build.sh`, with Docker:

1. `risk-calculator.R` is copied from `risk-score-service` into
   `nelarisk/inst/` (`cmp` checks the copy is exact; the copy is ignored by
   git). `nelarisk` is a two-function R package around it:
   `risk_pre(data)` and `risk_post(data)` source the file on first use and
   call `calculate_risk_score()` / `calculate_risk_score_post()`, as the
   plumber service does.
2. [rwasm](https://github.com/r-wasm/rwasm) compiles `nelarisk` and `dplyr`
   (and its 14 dependencies) for WebAssembly and packs them into one
   filesystem image, `dist/model/vfs/library.data` (12 MB). rwasm runs
   inside `ghcr.io/r-wasm/webr:main`, the image its documentation
   prescribes, which carries the Emscripten and Flang toolchain.
3. The matching webR runtime is copied out of the same image to
   `dist/model/webr/` (46 MB on disk, ~12 MB compressed over the wire), so
   runtime and packages are the same R (4.6).

`bun run build` runs it. Everything in `dist/` is static files.

## Proof

`bun run test` (Playwright, Chromium) serves `dist/` locally, starts R in
the page, and scores every row of the reference sheet and both ASC Audit
extracts in one `data.frame` each, against the scores the service gave:

| Sheet | Rows scored | Differ | Time |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `sim_data_v4` reference (pre-op) | 4,940 | 0 | 2.6 s |
| ASC Audit extract, pre-op | 3,352 | 0 | 1.0 s |
| ASC Audit extract, post-op | 3,266 | 0 | 0.9 s |

Rows the service refuses (an input missing) are the rows with no expected
score, and are checked to be so. R starts in about 1.3 s.

## In a page

```html
<script src="https://nela-risk-model.example.org/risk-r.js"></script>
<script>
  riskR.start({ modelUrl: 'https://nela-risk-model.example.org/model/' })
  riskR.compute('pre', payload).then(function (score) { /* 13.9, or null */ })
</script>
```

`payload` is what the page already posts to the service (`S01AgeOnArrival`,
`S03ASAScore`, … the `S03Ind_*` indications as 0/1, and the malignancy /
soiling / urgency fields of the score wanted). Values may be numbers or
strings. `compute` takes an array of payloads too and returns an array.
`start()` is called once, at page load, so the first score is ready sooner;
`compute()` waits for it when needed.

The ASC Audit pages (`docs/nela/old/EmLap-v12.js`, `EmLap-v13.js`,
`NoLap-v3.js`, `NoLap-v2.js`) have `RISK.engine` (`"r"` or `"service"`) and
`RISK.model` (this site's URL); their computed score fields call
`computeRisk()`, which uses R in the page when it is up and the service
otherwise - so the score is never simply absent. The computed field runs
it in the background either way: the page never waits, a newer set of
inputs abandons an older computation, and the value is posted with the
record and shared with a collaboration room like any other.

To put it on Domino: nothing to upload but the four page files; the model
is served from this site (Coolify app `nela-risk-model`, from the
Dockerfile here, which needs `dist/` built beforehand - `bun run build`,
then commit-free deploy of the built directory, or build on a runner with
Docker).

## Files

| File | What |
| --- | --- |
| `build.sh` | copies the R file, runs rwasm, copies the runtime out |
| `nelarisk/` | the R package around the supplied file (`inst/` filled at build) |
| `risk-r.js` | the page wrapper: `riskR.start()`, `riskR.compute()` |
| `parity.spec.ts` | the proof above |
| `index.html`, `Dockerfile`, `Caddyfile` | the static site that serves it |
| `dist/model/` | build output (ignored): `vfs/` image, `webr/` runtime |
